#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253605 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172041 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75710e99-e13c-54ba-9401-486bfec15284" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rectangular Regions Where a Slope Field Is Positive or Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e1be2fa-de0d-5f22-b440-911091c56105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437582} {:answer/id #uuid "75d08e9a-c55b-5a67-abb2-4e27159b9b63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e1be2fa-de0d-5f22-b440-911091c56105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437582} :answer-field/id #uuid "8390e0db-2166-50f2-a123-b7b9177c8341" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438820} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3164774-f189-596d-acdb-746f708a14aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437584} {:answer/id #uuid "e364779c-88b2-5f8d-ac35-11f4c01ba4f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3164774-f189-596d-acdb-746f708a14aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437584} :answer-field/id #uuid "a904fb7a-832f-5a30-ac49-1d6d8c3a62e6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438821} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b51910a4-e37d-5c34-adb4-b2218d1f40f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437586} {:answer/id #uuid "5ab61bfa-dc48-58d5-a149-9bf36c574b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b51910a4-e37d-5c34-adb4-b2218d1f40f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437586} :answer-field/id #uuid "71947ae8-7e46-57cd-b733-f67a0fa6d76c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dff46479-0340-5239-b8ff-db620f2c9a7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-119800" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(1-x)(y-2)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y>2,$ the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **II.** At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>1$ and $y<2,$ the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **III.** At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y<2,$ the slope of the slope field is positive" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=(1-x)(y-2).$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=1$ or $y=2.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/47/47784a3201e93648e495827b12078073cc9f1a03cd3c11904a875bad10a3bde2.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/73/73631c178777b4489e35fa87d08474ccf2b8b484b9bf5fe7272b1ce25d45f1b0.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $x<1$ and $y>2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $x>1$ and $y<2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement III is false. If $x<1$ and $y<2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253607 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172041 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75710e99-e13c-54ba-9401-486bfec15284" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rectangular Regions Where a Slope Field Is Positive or Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9e11f01-32e2-5138-b450-b28abfcfe393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437588} {:answer/id #uuid "eba29a8a-cdc7-5437-a377-49e424a33c92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9e11f01-32e2-5138-b450-b28abfcfe393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437588} :answer-field/id #uuid "6731a097-fbbb-5d0d-924d-44214b41bafb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438823} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67be040e-e5a2-539e-bae4-03679cb8d0dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437590} {:answer/id #uuid "989c32ec-026e-53bf-8bf8-04e72bb618bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "989c32ec-026e-53bf-8bf8-04e72bb618bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437591} :answer-field/id #uuid "27e31d3a-247b-506c-a5ca-66c30896d048" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438824} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ffef47e-2f1a-52ce-9ce8-8cc5126973d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437592} {:answer/id #uuid "82c17871-30b3-570d-9985-cbfb4030107c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82c17871-30b3-570d-9985-cbfb4030107c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437593} :answer-field/id #uuid "300b0a1c-8c14-56f6-b340-cad908fc709b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2a6ca6d7-d1ef-5811-9457-4d7cf9a54890" :question/math-academy-id "q-119816" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(x-2)^{2}(y+1)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **II.** At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **III.** At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=(x-2)^{2}(y+1).$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=2$ or $y=-1.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/ca/caa61190f1a5565c58838556529715c08f9f00402c6f4b3ccb99a914e748f198.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/d8/d836463631120853e05b3b5fb9e534822cf5611747a3eb17e22333901bfb8fd3.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $x>2$ and $y>-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172085 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "019e5a17-1aab-565b-8881-447c86a9a7ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Two-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dfdb090-b6f2-5639-aede-69a2ab60459d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437618} {:answer/id #uuid "8709f1c4-65e1-54b0-9d7e-fb1cb2bfbedf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8709f1c4-65e1-54b0-9d7e-fb1cb2bfbedf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437619} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8671b01-0de0-54e6-81e3-d9dce3d551cb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438838} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f49f49bb-0589-51e3-8307-793ca10c0906" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437620} {:answer/id #uuid "e78b01f6-8039-5eb5-a36a-b79ac0375eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e78b01f6-8039-5eb5-a36a-b79ac0375eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437621} :answer-field/id #uuid "811ad6c5-2f4c-5371-a120-40ade9271191" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438839} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "177eaf39-4c0c-56e2-b24b-1fe2e1490f63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437622} {:answer/id #uuid "3b92af76-e3cd-572a-82c2-a86f00b68ae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "177eaf39-4c0c-56e2-b24b-1fe2e1490f63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437622} :answer-field/id #uuid "1603ebdc-1768-5b01-b37c-c00c63150d1d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "82c19ae8-c5db-5680-ac18-77dd108b7959" :question/math-academy-id "q-122650" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $U(x,y)=⟨\\frac{1}{x+2},\\sqrt{x-y}⟩$\n- **II.** $V(x,y)=⟨x{e}^{y},1-y⟩$\n- **III.** $W(x,y,z)=⟨x,-y,-z⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $U(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ne -2,\\,x-y\\ge 0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $V(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $W(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172085 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "019e5a17-1aab-565b-8881-447c86a9a7ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Two-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a345da55-40a0-58c5-bd97-11513a3c18ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437624} {:answer/id #uuid "91b6594a-7883-5a7f-8bd5-9117346c6a52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91b6594a-7883-5a7f-8bd5-9117346c6a52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437625} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3809f3b-8813-5ce8-88cd-4a794a7f1292" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438841} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70f0c14d-a0ab-547c-aa1b-626d40c92945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437626} {:answer/id #uuid "93e5dc0c-b8a9-51a7-b679-0830b810940c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70f0c14d-a0ab-547c-aa1b-626d40c92945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437626} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecbb9997-28d7-57dd-8e3a-e4fbdf98e863" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c750739b-5adf-51bf-8122-bbc865b012bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437628} {:answer/id #uuid "16c760f1-2a00-532d-8ab5-17d51057a421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c750739b-5adf-51bf-8122-bbc865b012bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437628} :answer-field/id #uuid "23d9d23a-b11c-50ab-a519-b5ea13ec3cca" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "212db81f-3e39-5c00-88aa-953a8a56ffb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-122653" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y),\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)⟩$\n- **II.** $B(x,y,z)=⟨-2x,3{y}^{3},{z}^{5}⟩$\n- **III.** $C(t)=⟨2-{t}^{2},{e}^{t-1}⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $A(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x+y>0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $B(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $C(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$  It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256693 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172085 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "019e5a17-1aab-565b-8881-447c86a9a7ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Two-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "719148a4-d796-5d0f-bf37-0acb3355c237" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437642} {:answer/id #uuid "eba23c1d-3faf-5e1e-a91b-717c3d32e34d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eba23c1d-3faf-5e1e-a91b-717c3d32e34d" :answer/type 