:question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f63ae22-12f3-552d-bede-acf1007c6564" :question/math-academy-id "q-122678" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $U(x,y)=⟨(x+2){e}^{y},\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x-y}⟩$\n- **II.** $V(x,y,z)=⟨5,{x}^{3}y,1-{y}^{3}⟩$\n- **III.** $W(x,y)=⟨x-3{y}^{2},2-y⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $U(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ne y}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $K(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $V(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b794e8c-8662-57a3-9430-d2ee2d5efdaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437648} {:answer/id #uuid "4de84e82-6689-5660-adc6-f0c83536a456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4de84e82-6689-5660-adc6-f0c83536a456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437649} :answer-field/id #uuid "616c4d45-069a-5832-84ae-5f981fb6e66f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438853} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51aecfc3-403e-5cba-b3b7-254b2d3ff5c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437650} {:answer/id #uuid "1bb91534-359e-56df-b8a5-f99a590388aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51aecfc3-403e-5cba-b3b7-254b2d3ff5c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437650} :answer-field/id #uuid "f56d77cf-af96-5cc5-bb85-082f7d066b90" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438854} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfa28faf-de57-551e-91ac-c5848f304f1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437652} {:answer/id #uuid "8f649c81-72a4-5b3f-9b5f-758b4d86f2bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfa28faf-de57-551e-91ac-c5848f304f1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437652} :answer-field/id #uuid "61696c65-7ecb-5a3d-a4b0-3fd29e6ec63a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72c8972f-c700-5c53-9029-c1e143b47247" :question/math-academy-id "q-122685" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $T(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,j+{z}^{2}\\,k$\n- **II.** $U(t)=2t\\,i-{t}^{2}\\,j-\\sqrt{t}\\,k$\n- **III.** $V(x,y,z)={e}^{-2z}\\sqrt{x+y}$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $T(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point $(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}$ to a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $U(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $V(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{3}$ to functions in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256695 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a596d75-c886-5b2a-91fb-fb7040912254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437660} {:answer/id #uuid "14d600f9-2df6-53a0-baaf-26570d859584" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14d600f9-2df6-53a0-baaf-26570d859584" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437661} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdfc827e-4a82-5cd1-a5ae-5c66a06116d1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438859} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/