subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $U(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{3}$ to functions in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $V(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point $(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}$ to a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $W(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cd70e4d-6c48-57c7-9de7-29fb91ecd156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437672} {:answer/id #uuid "c8a035b0-a3e5-53be-a422-6c7151b90283" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cd70e4d-6c48-57c7-9de7-29fb91ecd156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437672} :answer-field/id #uuid "82f16859-809f-5571-9e24-04024074834c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438865} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84952cf5-bae9-566b-8785-0e7b44cb9f1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437674} {:answer/id #uuid "9499395a-41a6-544d-ae0b-b638a3373619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9499395a-41a6-544d-ae0b-b638a3373619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437675} :answer-field/id #uuid "16a42706-0e2c-5b8a-a048-2ec4e31f3fbc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438866} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df7e1c2f-9a73-51cd-b44a-97d3a3f06124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437676} {:answer/id #uuid "0039b744-c30f-5b87-90ae-3f6e231319ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0039b744-c30f-5b87-90ae-3f6e231319ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437677} :answer-field/id #uuid "28d18e6e-3fdd-511d-adcf-4ebf4d97e428" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438867}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "659f4527-cc88-5c6b-8485-f595eee1689f" :question/math-academy-id "q-122694" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $N(x,y)=⟨x{e}^{y},\\sqrt{x+y}⟩$\n- **II.** $P(x,y,z)=⟨{e}^{x-2y},\\sqrt{3-x},3{z}^{3}⟩$\n- **III.** $Q(x,y,z)=⟨-1,2,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x-y+z)⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $N(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $P(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,3-x\\ge 0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $Q(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,2x-y+z>0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "381ec827-a8d9-525e-879e-9867a01781c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437684} {:answer/id #uuid "49b34905-3523-5220-8445-649a78b38000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "381ec827-a8d9-525e-879e-9867a01781c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437684} :answer-field/id #uuid "18ab9680-7869-5328-9a15-6eba928afef1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438871} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87e56ee0-4b15-585a-b00b-9c198815d5c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437686} {:answer/id #uuid "8084195c-c80f-5724-a464-b4190c772af2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87e56ee0-4b15-585a-b00b-9c198815d5c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437686} :answer-field/id #uuid "f57b8a4e-6326-51ba-9d83-e214db0e9062" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438872} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9acb7596-f53f-56d2-b363-d2432bfdfc06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437688} {:answer/id #uuid "7cff525b-7dbd-51e3-9c41-4f3a63d8b105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cff525b-7dbd-51e3-9c41-4f3a63d8b105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437689} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee64c134-4670-5bcf-b390-f48716fc96b5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89ed8a40-4bb8-5a40-9a2c-1bf03637a8bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-122696" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $C(x,y,z)=\\frac{z}{x+y}$\n- **II.** $D(x,y)=⟨{y}^{3}-3,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y),7{x}^{3}⟩$\n- **III.** $E(x,y,z)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+z),\\operatorname{tan}⁡z,\\frac{1}{x-y}⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $C(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{3}$ to functions in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $D(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $E(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,x\\ne y,\\,z\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\\,n\\in Z}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133880 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Divergence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdadf6b7-b5f9-5ff7-9423-ee3c12b80906" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437696} {:answer/id #uuid "7afe5777-93e3-5e99-a2e4-41abc2620fde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdadf6b7-b5f9-5ff7-9423-ee3c12b80906" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437696} :answer-field/id #uuid "56b6426b-0fec-5055-bd39-2d631eea5084" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438877} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ee82610-209a-5b78-b3d9-815a176668e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437698} {:answer/id #uuid "218da758-973f-597f-9d25-7e96cca48a13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 1759