/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d890a9be-d244-5a2b-a434-390b31123a28" :question/math-academy-id "q-123245" :question/problem "![](images/b3/b315be9ba524ab538388fdaad31161c280d7d6e5ab71261345063ac6ffe819d5.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $∇\\cdot F=0$\n- **II.** $∇\\cdot F>0$\n- **III.** $∇\\cdot F<0$\n- **IV.** $F$ is solenoidal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statements I and III are false. Notice that the lengths of the vectors increase as we move vertically and horizontally away from the origin. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a source at every point.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259580 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166863 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "65adbd80-9647-59d8-bd4a-42f431587c85" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Conservative Vector Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71ea03ce-0bea-5a33-b768-531593cecfa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437710} {:answer/id #uuid "3e12d6c1-cf51-5a79-9824-a889289525f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71ea03ce-0bea-5a33-b768-531593cecfa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437710} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9705fa0-051d-5108-9f33-8e0b95bf6771" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438884} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71524ab4-c1fe-56a5-b9b0-5f1247ce034e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437712} {:answer/id #uuid "9809981f-9ddb-5aa8-be88-9c61eb732ec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9809981f-9ddb-5aa8-be88-9c61eb732ec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437713} :answer-field/id #uuid "57bc640c-07ec-54b1-ad03-d8c8b9f0a1f6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438885} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "425e03bd-f65f-5c5d-a11e-3e1e0b0bfa52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437714} {:answer/id #uuid "6312d848-ea3c-5408-9f3b-a4a431e27732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6312d848-ea3c-5408-9f3b-a4a431e27732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437715} :answer-field/id #uuid "482a8231-c447-5ba1-b319-c14d7a80bd76" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dc1786af-49ed-5f49-98af-90852a6f6e8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-123984" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,j$\n- **II.** $G=3{e}^{3x+2y}\\,i+2{e}^{3x+2y}\\,j$\n- **III.** $H=2xy\\,i+({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,j$" :question/worked-solution "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nNote that for each of our functions, $D={R}^{2}.$ With this in mind, let's check each of the vector fields. \n\n- For the vector field $F,$ we have $P=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ and $Q=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are not equal, we conclude that $F$ is not conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $G,$ we have $P=3{e}^{3x+2y}$ and $Q=2{e}^{3x+2y}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=6{e}^{3x+2y},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=6{e}^{3x+2y}.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $G$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $H,$ we have $P=2xy$ and $Q={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2x.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $H$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259827 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087713 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed7286fe-b6e2-5544-8bc6-86afc6cdb813" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Matrix by Its Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6de0a05e-35c3-57a9-a633-24feca8aec6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437728} {:answer/id #uuid "a3293c58-9876-5911-b70e-5bf77f356b9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6de0a05e-35c3-57a9-a633-24feca8aec6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437728} :answer-field/id #uuid "60cd9c02-72f4-5e39-ba16-e8546d305f38" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438893} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8d7e07c-fa2d-5b6e-9445-c270cbc53deb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437730} {:answer/id #uuid "3861251b-b788-5c0a-a947-970af5df7cbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3861251b-b788-5c0a-a947-970af5df7cbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437731} :answer-field/id #uuid "51f0d4c9-a62e-5721-ae74-a0d35fa895d9" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438894} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5faed2cd-4e29-51ed-80b8-f43cca55c3ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437732} {:answer/id #uuid "31a863f4-dd71-5c0f-94af-aee28bce10ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5faed2cd-4e29-51ed-80b8-f43cca55c3ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437732} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae2db61c-4f3b-5ee7-b7dd-921b0297ed48" :answer-field/key "D" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0cf927e3-7417-58b7-b060-c44ad3d85430" :question/math-academy-id "q-125552" :question/problem "Which of the following is a $2\\times 1$ matrix?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $B$ has $2$ rows and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $2\\times 2.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $2$ rows and $1$ column. So, its dimensions are $2\\times 1.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- The matrix $D$ has $1$ row and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $1\\times 2.$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262604 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119772 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b55b50a0-034f-57c0-8a61-883cfb0412dc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uui